  "seoBody": "<h2>Is Mitti the same as SafetyCulture?</h2><p>Yes. SafetyCulture rebranded as Mitti in August 2026. It is the same company, the same platform and the same pricing model, with Luke Anear continuing as chief executive. The product was called iAuditor before it was called SafetyCulture. If you compared SafetyCulture against alternatives before the rename, that comparison still holds against Mitti.</p><h2>Why do firms look for a Mitti alternative?</h2><p>Rarely because the product is weak. Mitti is the largest inspection platform in the market, with over two million users across 80,000 organisations and the broadest template library available. The two recurring reasons are adoption and price shape. It is an app that every worker must install and log into, and it is charged per seat, so you pay for every name on the account whether that person inspected anything this month or not.</p><h2>What does Quickler do differently?</h2><p>Two things. Checks arrive in the WhatsApp or Telegram already on the worker's phone, so there is nothing to install, no login and no training. And the finished record is written into your own report template, the Word or PDF document your firm already issues to clients, with your styles, headings, tables and logo kept. Most tools hand you their layout and leave the rebuild to you.</p><h2>How much does Quickler cost compared with Mitti?</h2><p>Quickler is £50 per phone number a month, with a £50 monthly minimum. A phone number counts when it did at least one check that month, so people who do nothing that month cost nothing. A 30-person team with 5 regular inspectors pays £250 a month. Per-seat tools charge for all 30 names. The honest limit: if nearly everyone in your firm inspects most days, per seat may be cheaper, and we will tell you so rather than lose you later.</p><h2>What does Mitti do that Quickler does not?</h2><p>A great deal. Training and onboarding, asset maintenance, contractor management, document control, lone worker safety, investigations, analytics with cross-site benchmarking, and insurance. Quickler is the capture and write-up layer only. If you want one platform to run frontline operations, Mitti is the stronger fit and we would say so.</p><h2>Can we try Quickler without committing?</h2><p>Yes. The free tier gives you 10 reports a month, up to 10 photos per report, unlimited users, free forever, with no card and no trial clock. Run your own Check through it alongside whatever you use now and compare the output.</p>",
